.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt ERR_SET_MARK 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ERR_set_mark ,
.Nm ERR_clear_last_mark ,
.Nm ERR_pop_to_mark ,
.Nm ERR_count_to_mark ,
.Nm ERR_pop
.Nd set mark, clear mark, pop errors until mark and pop last error
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/err.h
.Ft int
.Fo ERR_set_mark
.Fa void
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo ERR_pop_to_mark
.Fa void
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo ERR_clear_last_mark
.Fa void
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo ERR_count_to_mark
.Fa void
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo ERR_pop
.Fa void
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn ERR_set_mark
sets a mark on the current topmost error record if there is one.
.Pp
.Fn ERR_pop_to_mark
will pop the top of the error stack until a mark is found.
The mark is then removed.
If there is no mark, the whole stack is removed.
.Pp
.Fn ERR_clear_last_mark
removes the last mark added if there is one.
.Pp
.Fn ERR_count_to_mark
returns the number of entries on the error stack above the most recently
marked entry, not including that entry.
If there is no mark in the error stack, the number of entries in the
error stack is returned.
.Pp
.Fn ERR_pop
unconditionally pops a single error entry from the top of the error
stack (which is the entry obtainable via
.Xr ERR_peek_last_error 3 Ns ).
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn ERR_set_mark
returns 0 if the error stack is empty, otherwise 1.
.Pp
.Fn ERR_clear_last_mark
and
.Fn ERR_pop_to_mark
return 0 if there was no mark in the error stack, which implies that the
stack became empty, otherwise 1.
.Pp
.Fn ERR_count_to_mark
returns the number of error stack entries found above the most recent
mark, if any, or the total number of error stack entries.
.Pp
.Fn ERR_pop
returns 1 if an error was popped or 0 if the error stack was empty.
.Sh HISTORY
.Fn ERR_count_to_mark
was added in OpenSSL 3.2.
.Fn ERR_pop
was added in OpenSSL 3.3.
